### Configure Wrangler for Custom Dockerfile

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/configuration/dockerfile

Configures the Wrangler project to use a custom Dockerfile for the container environment. This tells Wrangler to build and use the specified Dockerfile when running or deploying the project.

```json
{
  "containers": [
    {
      "binding": "CONTAINER",
      "dockerfile": "./Dockerfile",
    },
  ],
}

```

--------------------------------

### Create Custom Sandbox Docker Image with Additional Packages

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/configuration/dockerfile

Extends the base sandbox Docker image by installing additional Python packages using pip, Node.js packages globally using npm, and system packages using apt-get. Ensure to clean up apt cache to reduce image size.

```dockerfile
FROM docker.io/cloudflare/sandbox:0.3.3


# Install additional Python packages
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir \
    scikit-learn==1.3.0 \
    tensorflow==2.13.0 \
    transformers==4.30.0


# Install Node.js packages globally
RUN npm install -g typescript ts-node prettier


# Install system packages
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
    postgresql-client \
    redis-tools \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

```

--------------------------------

### Execute Command with exec() in JavaScript/TypeScript

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/api/commands

Executes a command in the sandbox and returns the complete result. Supports streaming output via callbacks. It takes the command string and an optional options object for streaming and timeouts. Returns a promise resolving to an ExecuteResponse object containing success status, stdout, stderr, and exit code.

```javascript
const result = await sandbox.exec("npm run build");

if (result.success) {
  console.log("Build output:", result.stdout);
} else {
  console.error("Build failed:", result.stderr);
}


// With streaming
await sandbox.exec("npm install", {
  stream: true,
  onOutput: (stream, data) => console.log(`[${stream}] ${data}`)
});
```

```typescript
const result = await sandbox.exec('npm run build');


if (result.success) {
  console.log('Build output:', result.stdout);
} else {
  console.error('Build failed:', result.stderr);
}


// With streaming
await sandbox.exec('npm install', {
  stream: true,
  onOutput: (stream, data) => console.log(`[${stream}] ${data}`)
});
```

--------------------------------

### Filesystem Operations (Write Files, Execute Commands)

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/concepts/containers

Shows how to interact with the sandbox filesystem, including writing files to specific directories and executing shell commands like 'ls'.

```javascript
await sandbox.writeFile('/workspace/app.py', 'print("Hello")');
await sandbox.writeFile('/tmp/cache.json', '{}');
await sandbox.exec('ls -la /workspace');
```

--------------------------------

### Use Base Sandbox Docker Image

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/configuration/dockerfile

Specifies the base Docker image to use for the Cloudflare sandbox environment. It's crucial to match the Docker image version with the npm package version for consistency.

```dockerfile
FROM docker.io/cloudflare/sandbox:0.3.3

```

### Sandbox Initialization for User Isolation

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/concepts/containers

Provides an example of how to obtain a sandbox instance, potentially creating a new one with a specific identifier to ensure user isolation.

```javascript
const sandbox = getSandbox(env.Sandbox, `user-${userId}`);
```

--------------------------------

### Read files from Sandbox filesystem (JavaScript, TypeScript)

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/guides/manage-files

Demonstrates reading text, JSON, and binary files from the sandbox filesystem. It returns file content and supports specifying encoding for binary files. Requires an initialized sandbox instance.

```javascript
// Read text file
const file = await sandbox.readFile("/workspace/app.js");
console.log(file.content);


// Read and parse JSON
const configFile = await sandbox.readFile("/workspace/config.json");
const config = JSON.parse(configFile.content);


// Read binary file
const imageFile = await sandbox.readFile("/workspace/image.png", {
  encoding: "base64",
});
return new Response(atob(imageFile.content), {
  headers: { "Content-Type": "image/png" },
});
```

```typescript
// Read text file
const file = await sandbox.readFile('/workspace/app.js');
console.log(file.content);


// Read and parse JSON
const configFile = await sandbox.readFile('/workspace/config.json');
const config = JSON.parse(configFile.content);


// Read binary file
const imageFile = await sandbox.readFile('/workspace/image.png', { encoding: 'base64' });
return new Response(atob(imageFile.content), {
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'image/png' }
});
```

--------------------------------

### Start Background Process with startProcess() in JavaScript/TypeScript

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/api/commands

Starts a long-running process in the background within the sandbox. It takes the command string and an optional options object for specifying the working directory and environment variables. It returns a promise resolving to a ProcessInfo object containing the process ID and status.

```javascript
const server = await sandbox.startProcess("python -m http.server 8000");
console.log("Started with PID:", server.pid);


// With custom environment
const app = await sandbox.startProcess("node app.js", {
  cwd: "/workspace/my-app",
  env: { NODE_ENV: "production", PORT: "3000" },
});
```

```typescript
const server = await sandbox.startProcess('python -m http.server 8000');
console.log('Started with PID:', server.pid);


// With custom environment
const app = await sandbox.startProcess('node app.js', {
  cwd: '/workspace/my-app',
  env: { NODE_ENV: 'production', PORT: '3000' }
});
```

--------------------------------

### Start Background Process - startProcess()

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/api/commands

Start a long-running background process within the sandbox.

```APIDOC
## POST /sandbox/startProcess

### Description
Start a long-running background process.

### Method
POST

### Endpoint
`/sandbox/startProcess`

### Parameters
#### Request Body
- **command** (string) - Required - The command to start as a background process.
- **options** (object) - Optional - Options for starting the process.
  - **cwd** (string) - Optional - Working directory for the process.
  - **env** (object) - Optional - Environment variables for the process.

### Request Example
```json
{
  "command": "python -m http.server 8000",
  "options": {
    "cwd": "/app",
    "env": {
      "PORT": "3000"
    }
  }
}
```

### Response
#### Success Response (200)
- **id** (string) - Unique identifier for the process.
- **pid** (number) - The process ID (PID) of the background process.
- **command** (string) - The command that was started.
- **status** (string) - The current status of the process (e.g., 'running').

#### Response Example
```json
{
  "id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-1234-567890abcdef",
  "pid": 12345,
  "command": "python -m http.server 8000",
  "status": "running"
}
```
```

--------------------------------

### Execute Command - exec()

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/api/commands

Execute a command and return the complete result, including standard output and error.

```APIDOC
## POST /sandbox/exec

### Description
Execute a command and return the complete result.

### Method
POST

### Endpoint
`/sandbox/exec`

### Parameters
#### Request Body
- **command** (string) - Required - The command to execute (can include arguments)
- **options** (object) - Optional - Options for command execution
  - **stream** (boolean) - Optional - Enable streaming callbacks (default: `false`)
  - **onOutput** (function) - Optional - Callback for real-time output: `(stream: 'stdout' | 'stderr', data: string) => void`
  - **timeout** (number) - Optional - Maximum execution time in milliseconds

### Request Example
```json
{
  "command": "npm run build",
  "options": {
    "stream": true,
    "onOutput": "(stream, data) => console.log(`[${stream}] ${data}`)"
  }
}
```

### Response
#### Success Response (200)
- **success** (boolean) - Indicates if the command executed successfully.
- **stdout** (string) - The standard output of the command.
- **stderr** (string) - The standard error of the command.
- **exitCode** (number) - The exit code of the command.

#### Response Example
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "stdout": "Build output: ...",
  "stderr": "",
  "exitCode": 0
}
```
```

### Create Directory API

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/api/files

Create a directory in the sandbox filesystem.

```APIDOC
## mkdir()

### Description
Create a directory in the sandbox filesystem.

### Method
POST (simulated)

### Endpoint
/sandbox/mkdir

### Parameters
#### Request Body
- **path** (string) - Required - Absolute path to the directory.
- **options** (object) - Optional - Directory creation options.
  - **recursive** (boolean) - Optional - Create parent directories if needed (default: `false`).

### Request Example
```json
{
  "path": "/workspace/src"
}
```
```json
{
  "path": "/workspace/src/components/ui",
  "options": {
    "recursive": true
  }
}
```

### Response
#### Success Response (200)
- **void** - Indicates successful directory creation.

#### Response Example
(No specific response body for success)
```

--------------------------------

### Manage Files in Sandbox Filesystem

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/index

This snippet illustrates file operations within the sandbox environment. It demonstrates creating a directory recursively, writing content to a file, and then reading the file's content back using the Sandbox SDK.

```typescript
import { getSandbox } from '@cloudflare/sandbox';


export default {
  async fetch(request: Request, env: Env): Promise<Response> {
    const sandbox = getSandbox(env.Sandbox, 'user-123');


    // Create a project structure
    await sandbox.mkdir('/workspace/project/src', { recursive: true });


    // Write files
    await sandbox.writeFile(
      '/workspace/project/package.json',
      JSON.stringify({ name: 'my-app', version: '1.0.0' })
    );


    // Read a file back
    const content = await sandbox.readFile('/workspace/project/package.json');


    return Response.json({ content });
  }
};

```

--------------------------------

### Write multiple files in parallel in Sandbox (JavaScript, TypeScript)

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/guides/manage-files

Demonstrates writing multiple files concurrently within the sandbox filesystem using `Promise.all` and `sandbox.writeFile`. This is useful for optimizing the writing of several files at once. Requires an initialized sandbox instance.

```javascript
const files = {
  "/workspace/src/app.js": 'console.log("app");',
  "/workspace/src/utils.js": 'console.log("utils");',
  "/workspace/README.md": "# My Project",
};


await Promise.all(
  Object.entries(files).map(([path, content]) =>
    sandbox.writeFile(path, content),
  ),
);

```

```typescript
const files = {
  '/workspace/src/app.js': 'console.log("app");',
  '/workspace/src/utils.js': 'console.log("utils");',
  '/workspace/README.md': '# My Project'
};


await Promise.all(
  Object.entries(files).map(([path, content]) =>
    sandbox.writeFile(path, content)
  )
);

```

--------------------------------

### Create Directory and Write File in Cloudflare Sandbox

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/guides/manage-files

Shows how to create a directory, including parent directories if they don't exist, and then write a file to that directory within the Cloudflare Sandbox. This is useful for organizing files. Available in JavaScript and TypeScript.

```javascript
// Create directory, then write file
await sandbox.mkdir("/workspace/data", { recursive: true });
await sandbox.writeFile("/workspace/data/file.txt", content);
```

```typescript
// Create directory, then write file
await sandbox.mkdir('/workspace/data', { recursive: true });
await sandbox.writeFile('/workspace/data/file.txt', content);
```

--------------------------------

### Create directory in sandbox

Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/api/files

Creates a directory at the specified path in the sandbox filesystem. Supports recursive creation of parent directories. Takes the directory path and optional recursive flag as parameters.

```javascript
await sandbox.mkdir("/workspace/src");


// Nested directories
await sandbox.mkdir("/workspace/src/components/ui", { recursive: true });
```

```typescript
await sandbox.mkdir('/workspace/src');


// Nested directories
await sandbox.mkdir('/workspace/src/components/ui', { recursive: true });
```

